## languages

recently ive taken a liking for C. either way, heres the languages that i like
and use constantly:

- [c99](https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/WG14/www/docs/n1256.pdf): the bestest language ever
- [zig](https://ziglang.org/): second bestest language ever, 1.0 tomorrow
- [posix shell](https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/utilities/V3_chap02.html)

and heres some more that i have adequate experience with:

- [golang](https://go.dev/): mostly for web projects because it has an awesome
  concurrency model and all that.
- [rust](https://rust-lang.org/): its fast, and if you like pain its also safe
- [python3](https://python.org/): i just used it for 3 whole years straight im
  good at it i think

and some miscellaneous generic stuff like:

- generic webdev stuff like html/css/js
- better webdev stuff like [typescript](https://www.typescriptlang.org/),
  [scss](https://sass-lang.com/) and [tailwind](https://tailwindcss.com/)
- frameworks like [svelte](https://svelte.dev/)
  (+[sveltekit](https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/introduction)),
  [solidjs](https://solidjs.org/), and [astro](https://astro.build/)

